  "text": "Here's a nicer idea: let the walls do the heavy lifting. Instead of that extra distribution layer, you use the walls themselves to carry the load basically turn them into beams. Wall-beams. There's a catch, of course: once a wall is carrying load, you can't just punch a big opening in it wherever you feel like it. So you have to think about the walls together, floor by floor line up the openings and the load paths. And the moment you do that, layout and structure stop being two separate problems. They're locked together. You can't design one without the other.",
