  "sentences": [
    {
      "text": "Here's a nicer idea: let the walls do the heavy lifting.",
      "start": 0.099,
      "end": 3.139
    },
    {
      "text": "Instead of that extra distribution layer, you use the walls themselves to carry the load basically turn them into beams.",
      "start": 3.419,
      "end": 9.619
    },
    {
      "text": "Wall-beams.",
      "start": 9.939,
      "end": 10.599
    },
    {
      "text": "There's a catch, of course: once a wall is carrying load, you can't just punch a big opening in it wherever you feel like it.",
      "start": 10.96,
      "end": 16.799
    },
    {
      "text": "So you have to think about the walls together, floor by floor line up the openings and the load paths.",
      "start": 16.879,
      "end": 21.959
    },
    {
      "text": "And the moment you do that, layout and structure stop being two separate problems.",
      "start": 22.0,
      "end": 26.239
    },
    {
      "text": "They're locked together.",
      "start": 26.299,
      "end": 27.439
    },
    {
      "text": "You can't design one without the other.",
      "start": 27.479,
